// D1566 — an OPERATOR over an element of an unpinned `__array_new_default__`. Sibling of
// D1470's matrix, which grades the same intrinsic at a NON-i32 element; this one grades the
// i32 default itself, reached through an operator operand rather than a store.
//
// THE PROOF USES ALL THREE OPERAND POSITIONS ON PURPOSE. `print(v[0])` alone runs in BOTH
// faces (nothing indexes `T.tys` with the element type, and the emitter reads the row after the
// flush pinned it), so a read-only proof passes on the very defect this row exists to catch.
// And a LEFT-operand-only proof passes on the `lt < 0` guard alone — the guard suppresses the
// arms, and the emitter still resolves the row. Only the RIGHT operand and the UNARY one need
// the operand peek, so all three are here or the template cannot tell the two fixes apart.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@VALUE@@
__array_new_default__(3)
// @@TYPE@@
i32[]
// @@PROOF@@
print(v[0] + 1)
print(1 + v[0])
print(-v[0])
// @@WANT@@
1 then 1 then 0
